tional perturbation models that generalize across multiple CRISPR systems and cell types\",\n          \"Build gene regulatory network-aware latent variable models that incorporate epigenomic and TF binding data\",\n          \"Explore diffusion-based generative models for perturbation response prediction\",\n          \"Use foundation models for single-cell transcriptomics as encoders for perturbation prediction\"\n        ],\n        \"biological_validation\": [\n          \"Validate predicted top DE genes against bulk RNA-seq of the same K562 CRISPRi perturbations\",\n          \"Compare predicted perturbation effect sizes with DepMap CRISPR gene dependency scores\",\n          \"Test whether predicted downstream signatures recover known TF and gene modules\",\n          \"Perform independent qPCR or Perturb-seq validation for selected perturbations\"\n        ],\n        \"clinical_translation\": [\n          \"Extend the model to predict patient-derived cell responses for drug target validation\",\n          \"Use perturbation effect predictions to prioritize CRISPR targets that mimic disease gene programs\",\n          \"Integrate predicted transcriptomic consequences with existing drug response models\",\n          \"Develop uncertainty-aware ranking for in vivo CRISPR screening follow-up\"\n        ],\n        \"technical_advancements\": [\n          \"Scale graph neural network training to full transcriptome gene sets\",\n          \"Integrate multi-modal data including chromatin accessibility and TF binding\",\n          \"Improve model calibration for rare and lowly expressed genes\",\n          \"Develop transfer learning from cell line data to primary tissue perturbations\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nPlease provide refinement comments in the following JSON format, incorporating decision support considerations:\n{\n    \"dataset\": {\n        \"biological\": {\n            \"relevance\": {\n                \"assessment\": \"string\",\n        