ll-molecule and genetic perturbations.\\\",\\n          \\\"SAMS-VAE\\\": \\\"Structure-aware multi-task VAE for single-cell perturbation data.\\\",\\n          \\\"Contrastive learning-based perturbation predictors\\\": \\\"Use contrastive objectives to align perturbation-induced expression changes with biological annotations.\\\",\\n          \\\"Graph neural network-based gene regulatory models\\\": \\\"Encode known gene regulatory interactions to constrain predicted expression changes.\\\",\\n          \\\"Linear or ridge regression on pseudobulk differential expression\\\": \\\"Regularized linear mapping from perturbation identity to mean expression delta.\\\",\\n          \\\"KNN or mean control baseline\\\": \\\"Predicts no change or average change using nearest neighbor or global control mean.\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"strengths\\\": [\\n          \\\"scGen and CPA provide out-of-distribution perturbation predictions using latent space arithmetic\\\",\\n          \\\"GEARS incorporates gene-gene relationships via co-expression and Gene Ontology graphs\\\",\\n          \\\"CPA and ChemCPA are scalable and support multiple perturbations and cell lines\\\",\\n          \\\"Variational autoencoder latent spaces can capture biological variation beyond technical noise\\\",\\n          \\\"Graph-based models can prioritize genes with known regulatory interactions\\\",\\n          \\\"Pseudobulk mean baselines are computationally cheap and can perform well for top DE gene ranking\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n          \\\"Many VAE-based methods struggle with unseen perturbations when effect directions are not represented in training\\\",\\n          \\\"GEARS relies on prior gene-gene interaction graphs that may be incomplete or biased in K562\\\",\\n          \\\"scGen assumes additive perturbation effects in latent space, which may fail for strong CRISPRi knockdowns\\\",\\n          \\\"Most deep models are evaluated on seen perturbatio